## CODE QUALITY STANDARDS - ZERO TOLERANCE

### 1. ERROR HANDLING
- Never use bare `except:` - always specify exception types
- Always use `self.utils.page.extract_TestCaseFailed(e)` in catch blocks
- Use custom exceptions from `src.utils.core.exceptions`

### 2. CHECKLIST PATTERN (MANDATORY)
```python
mainChecklist = [
    "First verification point",
    "Second verification point",
]
subAutoTestCase = ''
indexChl = 0

# For each checklist item:
subAutoTestCase += f"- Description of what is being verified \n"
# Logic here
self.utils.update_result_to_ggsheet(
    Data["TestCase_spread_sheet_id"], 
    mainChecklist[indexChl], 
    testcase, 
    subAutoTestCase, 
    Data["TestCase_Auto_Status"][0],
    sheet_name=Checklist_Sheet_Name
)
indexChl += 1
subAutoTestCase = ''
```

### 3. ASSERTION METHODS
- Use `self.utils.should_be_equal()` instead of assert
- Use `self.utils.should_be_true()` for boolean checks
- Use `self.utils.should_contain()` for string checks

### 4. WAIT PATTERNS
- Use `self.utils.page.wait_for_page_loaded()`
- Use `self.utils.page.wait_for_element_ready()`
- Use `self.utils.page.verify_element_exist()`

### 5. DATA ACCESS
- Use `self.utils.page.get_text()` for text extraction
- Use `self.utils.page.get_attribute()` for attributes
- Use `self.utils.page.get_element()` for element references

### 6. BROWSER ACTIONS
- Use `self.utils.page.click()` for clicks
- Use `self.utils.page.input()` for text input
- Use `self.utils.page.select_options()` for dropdowns